In sum and substance, absolutely NOTHING about Hallowe'en relates to what God considers pure/holy/godly in any way. 

As a very real example, I would never permit my sons, when they lived at home, to participate in the "Trick or Treat" part. "Tricking" is threatening some evil action/damage etc. if you are not furnished with candy ... a "treat". Neither action reflects godliness!

The *Lord* made the day, sure, it is His created time on watch ... man-kind co-opted that and made a mockery of Truth and of Holiness in general.

Thus, why I won't participate ... ever. (I leave my porch/driveway lights on because they are on all night throughout the year, but my screen door is closed.) I do not dress up, "costumes", etc.  We *MIGHT* carve pumpkins if suitable ones are around over this weekend, if not we will forego ...

But please don't use this day to promote Christ; even giving candy away to do that is, in reality, subversion.
It isn't honoring the day the way God intended. Let those who are walking in Darkness continue as they might (the wicked must grow more wicked) ... we do not have to join hands with unrighteousness ... as I see it.

</p><p id=220 pid=517 uid=A>This is the greatest load of legalism since Jesus walked on earth.  You said it yourself the “Lord made the day.”</p><p id=623 pid=220 uid=C139>Legalism? Hardly. It's the conviction of my heart. If doing what God desires is considered legalism, then those of us adhering as closely to doing things right must all be. This is pure rebellion to take a "custom" of man to subvert what God has ordained to be true -- why promote what isn't?

It has been long understood in the Church not to mingle with unrighteousness in all things ... let no one be enticed with evil of any kind. 

We are exhorted to pursue what fulfills godliness in us -- 2Peter 1:3-4 shows us this is precisely what He provides us: "As His divine power has given to us all things that pertain to life and godliness, through the knowledge of Him who called us by glory and virtue, by which have been given to us exceedingly great and precious promises, that through these you may be partakers of the divine nature, having escaped the corruption that is in the world through lust."

But here God makes clear our course, no matter the obstacle of mankind's 'ideas', from Philippians 4:8, (with added italics)

"Finally, brethren, whatever things are ***true***, whatever things are ***noble***, whatever things are ***just***, whatever things are ***pure***, whatever things are ***lovely***, whatever things are ***of good report***, if there is ***any virtue*** and if there is ***anything praiseworthy***—meditate on these things."

Is it "lovely" to wear costumes showing blood or murder, or witches or evil? "true" ? "noble"? "virtue" ?

How about God's point of view on mankind, from Proverbs 8:13 --  ***" The fear of the Lord is to hate evil; pride and arrogance and the evil way and the perverse mouth I hate."***

He's not interested in "partying" it up by those who celebrate those things ...


